(i)
providing that a judge of the Provincial Court to whom a complaint has been made, alleging that a animal has bitten or attempted to bite a person, may summon the owner of the animal to appear and to show cause why the animal should not be destroyed and may, if from the evidence produced it appears that the animal has bitten or has attempted to bite a person, make an order directing

(i)
that the animal be destroyed, or

(ii)
